cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ScoreQuant, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ScoreQuant: information-preserving binning for statistical inference"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for assigning observations to a few hard bins while retaining Fisher
  information about model parameters, by D-optimal and profiled D_s partitioning of score
  vectors.
authors:
  - family-names: Vorobyev
    given-names: Vitaly
    email: vit.vorobiev@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # to be added by the author
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/VitalyVorobyev/scorequant"
url: "https://vitalyvorobyev.github.io/scorequant/"
keywords:
  - binning
  - Fisher information
  - D-optimality
  - JAX
  - statistics
